WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:04.910
You have one server, and several apps that use Supabase.

00:04.960 --> 00:08.784
A full Supabase for each app fills its memory fast.

00:09.352 --> 00:12.459
And one shared project mixes everyone's data.

00:12.508 --> 00:18.563
Sbarbase turns the server into one building. Postgres runs once, in the basement.

00:18.882 --> 00:25.382
Each client is a floor, each project an apartment, and each environment a window with its own database.

00:25.432 --> 00:30.317
One engine for all of them leaves room for many more projects on the same server.

00:30.367 --> 00:36.260
Every request carries its environment's key, and the gateway sends it only to its own data.

00:36.310 --> 00:39.768
A key from one project never opens another.

00:39.817 --> 00:44.712
When one project gets busy, it gets its own share, and no more.

00:44.762 --> 00:50.350
Extra requests are told to try again shortly, and the other projects stay fast.

00:50.714 --> 00:53.498
One command installs it on the server you already have.

00:53.605 --> 00:58.164
Sbarbase. Many Supabase projects, one server.
